<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Josiah Harmar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1753–1813</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/josiah">Josiah</a> Harmar (1753–1813) was an American officer of the Revolutionary War who served as the senior officer of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> Army from 1784 to 1791. In October 1790 he led an expedition of regulars and militia against the Miami and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shawnee">Shawnee</a> towns near present-day Fort Wayne, Indiana, but his detachments were defeated by warriors under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/little-turtle">Little Turtle</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/blue-jacket">Blue Jacket</a>, a setback known as Harmar's Defeat.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/josiah-harmar.jpg" alt="Josiah Harmar" width="320" height="380" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Painting by Raphaelle Peale, photo of painting by Will Brown. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Josiah_Harmar_by_Raphaelle_Peale.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
